# These are OVERLAYS: they are laid over the feast's ordinary Common (alterius Temporis), which still
# gives the prayer, the lessons, and every part not named here.  Rules common to all of them:
#   Matins has ONE nocturn: invit, hymn, one antiphon (mat.ant) over three psalms with the V. of the
#   ordinary Common's nocturn chosen by weekday (Sun/Mon/Thu: I, Tue/Fri: II, Wed/Sat: III); the
#   benedictions before the lessons follow the same order; three lessons; three responsories.
#   For a Saint of the Order (op_rule): three antiphons of the I Nocturn of the ordinary Common with
